ields from the provider profile — a successful sign-in that routes back to an identical-looking page reads as a broken login.\\n- SSE chat: `fetch` + `res.body.getReader()`; normalize `\\\\r` out of the buffer **before** splitting frames — sse-starlette writes CRLF line endings and a chunk boundary can split `\\\\r\\\\n`; `.replace(/\\\\r/g, \\\"\\\")` then split on `\\\\n\\\\n` survives both. Events: `meta`, `token`, `sentence`, `done`, `error`. HTTP `402` = paywall gate (show the paywall, not an error), `503` = integration key missing server-side.\\n- Voice: enqueue sequence-numbered sentence jobs BEFORE asynchronous TTS completion; queuing URLs in promise completion order scrambles speech. Play serially, advance after `play()` rejection, and cancel/discard pending callbacks on mute/unmount. Test reversed synthesis latency and rejected autoplay. iOS grants the playback gesture privilege PER AUDIO ELEMENT, so one long-lived element must play everything — the unlock primer and every clip; a throwaway primer element earns nothing for the element that actually plays, and a blocked clip must STAY at the queue head (cache its synthesized URL, park the queue, replay it from the tap inside `unlock()`) — deleting it on block is silent voice death on iPhone. Settle the play frame on pause too, or stop()/mute strands one async frame per interruption. If the backend emits `sentence` but no `token` frames, render incremental text from `sentence` too; require a terminal `done`/`error` so premature SSE EOF is not silent success.\\n- Signed storage URLs expire: render via plain `<img>`/`<audio>` with an `absUrl()` prefix helper; don't route them through next/image.\\n\\n## Design (user's bar — generic dark + amber reads as unfinished)\\n- Commit to one surface per page before styling (landing = Decide, onboard = Configure, chat = Operate, paywall = Compare, keepsake = Explore); never reuse the centered-hero + equal-cards composition outside Decide.\\n- System that passed review: Fraunces display + Inter body via Google Fonts import in globals.css; Tailwind v4 @theme tokens (void #0b0908, ink #f2ede3, ember #e2a93b); film-grain overlay, hairline borders, one accent.\\n- Sticky translucent headers must be ≥95% opaque or scrolled content bleeds through the blur.\\n- Chat empty state must be vertically centered (flex h-full items-center justify-center), not top-pinned — top-pinned reads as broken.\\n- Chat threads must not sweep on open: anchor the list at the newest turn on mount (`listRef.scrollTop = listRef.scrollHeight`, no smooth) and fade the panel in once (`.chat-panel-in`); glide only for turns that arrive after mount, and stop auto-scrolling once the reader has scrolled up (stick-to-bottom flag recomputed on scroll, within ~120px of the end). Never put `scroll-smooth` on the message list — it animates the initial jump too.\\n- Composer: auto-grow the textarea to a max height, show the character counter only past a threshold (and always when <500 left), block send past the cap, and keep the client cap and the server cap in sync (comment each with the other file's constant).\\n- Brand assets...", "duration_ms": 213, "is_error": false, "timestamp": 1791119383933}
